T*
(* Periodic Functions: A function f\(x\) is periodic with period T if f\(x + T\) = f\(x\)) Tj
T*
(for all x in its domain.) Tj
T*
(* Dirichlet's Conditions for Fourier Convergence: Any function f\(x\) defined in) Tj
T*
(interval \(-c, c\) can be expanded into a convergent Fourier series provided:) Tj
T*
(1. f\(x\) is periodic, single-valued, and bounded.) Tj
T*
(2. f\(x\) has at most a finite number of jump discontinuities in any single period.) Tj
T*
(3. f\(x\) has at most a finite number of local maxima and minima in any single period.) Tj
T*
(* Convergence at Discontinuities: At a point of finite discontinuity x0, the Fourier) Tj
T*
(series converges to the arithmetic mean of its left- and right-hand limits: f\(x0\) = [) Tj
T*
(f\(x0-\) + f\(x0+\) ] / 2.) Tj
