([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Fourier Series of Square Wave and Gregory-Leibniz Formula]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Obtain the Fourier series for the square wave function defined by f\(x\) = -k for) Tj
T*
(-pi < x < 0, and f\(x\) = +k for 0 < x < pi, with f\(x + 2*pi\) = f\(x\). Hence deduce the) Tj
T*
(Gregory-Leibniz series: 1 - 1/3 + 1/5 - 1/7 + ... = pi / 4.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Symmetry inspection: f\(-x\) = -f\(x\). Thus f\(x\) is an ODD function.) Tj
T*
(Consequently: a0 = 0 and an = 0 for all n.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Fourier sine coefficients bn:) Tj
T*
(bn = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi f\(x\) * sin\(nx\) dx = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi k * sin\(nx\) dx) Tj
T*
(bn = \(2*k / pi\) * [ -cos\(nx\) / n ]_0^pi = \(2*k / \(n*pi\)\) * [ 1 - cos\(n*pi\) ].) Tj
T*
(Since cos\(n*pi\) = \(-1\)^n:) Tj
T*
(- If n is EVEN: 1 - \(-1\)^n = 1 - 1 = 0 => bn = 0.) Tj
T*
(- If n is ODD: 1 - \(-1\)^n = 1 - \(-1\) = 2 => bn = 4*k / \(n*pi\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Write out Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = \(4*k / pi\) * [ sin\(x\) + sin\(3x\)/3 + sin\(5x\)/5 + sin\(7x\)/7 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Deduce numerical sum at x = pi/2:) Tj
T*
(At x = pi/2, f\(pi/2\) = k.) Tj
T*
(sin\(pi/2\) = 1, sin\(3*pi/2\) = -1, sin\(5*pi/2\) = 1, sin\(7*pi/2\) = -1.) Tj
T*
(Substitute: k = \(4*k / pi\) * [ 1 - 1/3 + 1/5 - 1/7 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(Divide by k and multiply by pi/4:) Tj
T*
(1 - 1/3 + 1/5 - 1/7 + ... = pi / 4. \(Hence Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 2: Fourier Expansion of Parabolic Function f\(x\) = x^2]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Find the Fourier series of f\(x\) = x^2 in the interval -pi <= x <= pi. Hence) Tj
T*
(prove that:) Tj
T*
(1/1^2 - 1/2^2 + 1/3^2 - 1/4^2 + ... = pi^2 / 12, and 1/1^2 + 1/2^2 + 1/3^2 + ... = pi^2) Tj
T*
(/ 6.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Function parity: f\(-x\) = \(-x\)^2 = x^2 = f\(x\). f\(x\) is EVEN.) Tj
T*
(Therefore: bn = 0 for all n.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate a0:) Tj
T*
(a0 = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x^2 dx = \(2 / pi\) * [ x^3 / 3 ]_0^pi = \(2 / pi\) * \(pi^3 / 3\) =) Tj
T*
(2*pi^2 / 3.) Tj
T*
(Constant term: a0 / 2 = pi^2 / 3.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate an using integration by parts:) Tj
T*
(an = \(2 / pi\) * int_0^pi x^2 * cos\(nx\) dx.) Tj
T*
(Let u = x^2, dv = cos\(nx\) dx => v = sin\(nx\)/n, v1 = -cos\(nx\)/n^2, v2 = -sin\(nx\)/n^3.) Tj
T*
