(Using generalized parts: int u*v dx = u*v - u'*v1 + u''*v2) Tj
T*
(= [ x^2 * \(sin\(nx\)/n\) - \(2x\)*\(-cos\(nx\)/n^2\) + \(2\)*\(-sin\(nx\)/n^3\) ]_0^pi.) Tj
T*
(Evaluating at 0 and pi: sin\(n*pi\) = 0, so only cosine term survives:) Tj
T*
(an = \(2 / pi\) * [ 2*pi * cos\(n*pi\) / n^2 ] = \(4 / n^2\) * \(-1\)^n.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Write Fourier Series:) Tj
T*
(x^2 = pi^2 / 3 + 4 * sum_{n=1}^inf [ \(\(-1\)^n / n^2\) * cos\(nx\) ]) Tj
T*
(x^2 = pi^2 / 3 - 4 * [ cos\(x\)/1^2 - cos\(2x\)/2^2 + cos\(3x\)/3^2 - cos\(4x\)/4^2 + ... ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Deduction 1 \(Set x = 0\):) Tj
T*
(0 = pi^2 / 3 - 4 * [ 1/1^2 - 1/2^2 + 1/3^2 - 1/4^2 + ... ]) Tj
T*
(=> 4 * [ 1/1^2 - 1/2^2 + 1/3^2 - 1/4^2 + ... ] = pi^2 / 3) Tj
T*
(=> 1/1^2 - 1/2^2 + 1/3^2 - 1/4^2 + ... = pi^2 / 12. \(Proven\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 6: Deduction 2 \(Set x = pi\):) Tj
T*
(pi^2 = pi^2 / 3 - 4 * [ -1/1^2 - 1/2^2 - 1/3^2 - ... ] = pi^2 / 3 + 4 * [ 1/1^2 + 1/2^2) Tj
T*
(+ 1/3^2 + ... ]) Tj
T*
(pi^2 - pi^2 / 3 = 2*pi^2 / 3 = 4 * sum_{n=1}^inf \(1 / n^2\)) Tj
T*
(=> sum_{n=1}^inf \(1 / n^2\) = \(2*pi^2 / 3\) / 4 = pi^2 / 6. \(Basel Problem Proven\).) Tj
