(Problem: Find the half-range Fourier sine series for f\(x\) = x in the interval 0 < x < 2) Tj
T*
(\(L = 2\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: For half-range sine series, a0 = 0 and an = 0.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute bn with L = 2:) Tj
T*
(bn = \(2 / L\) * int_0^L f\(x\) * sin\(n*pi*x / L\) dx = \(2 / 2\) * int_0^2 x * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\)) Tj
T*
(dx.) Tj
T*
(bn = int_0^2 x * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) dx.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Integrate by parts \(u = x, dv = sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) dx\):) Tj
T*
(v = - [ 2 / \(n*pi\) ] * cos\(n*pi*x / 2\).) Tj
T*
(bn = [ - x * \(2 / \(n*pi\)\) * cos\(n*pi*x / 2\) ]_0^2 - int_0^2 [ - \(2 / \(n*pi\)\) *) Tj
T*
(cos\(n*pi*x / 2\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(bn = [ - 2 * \(2 / \(n*pi\)\) * cos\(n*pi\) - 0 ] + [ 4 / \(n^2*pi^2\) * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) ]_0^2.) Tj
T*
(Since sin\(n*pi\) = 0 and sin\(0\) = 0, the second bracket is zero.) Tj
T*
(bn = - \(4 / \(n*pi\)\) * \(-1\)^n = \(4 / \(n*pi\)\) * \(-1\)^{n+1}.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Write series expansion:) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = sum_{n=1}^inf [ \(4 / \(n*pi\)\) * \(-1\)^{n+1} * sin\(n*pi*x / 2\) ]) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = \(4 / pi\) * [ sin\(pi*x/2\) - \(1/2\)*sin\(2*pi*x/2\) + \(1/3\)*sin\(3*pi*x/2\) - ... ].) Tj
